1. A computer-implemented method comprising:

receiving, by one or more processors, a video stream having original video timing;

generating, by the one or more processors, a delayed video stream by delaying the video stream by a video delay interval;

transmitting the delayed video stream to a plurality of viewer devices for playback;

transmitting the video stream having the original video timing to a subtitling system;

receiving, from the subtitling system, subtitle data corresponding to the video stream;

receiving a subtitle delay signal indicative of a timing offset between the subtitle data and the delayed video stream;

adjusting presentation timing of the subtitle data based at least in part on the subtitle delay signal; and

providing the adjusted subtitle data for presentation with the delayed video stream at the plurality of viewer devices such that the subtitle data is synchronized with corresponding video content in the delayed video stream.

1. A communication network system comprising:

a video source configured to transmit an original video through a communication network;

a delay unit configured to receive the original video from the video source and to output a delayed video delayed by a predetermined delay time relative to the original video;

a subtitler terminal coupled to the communication network and configured to receive at least one of the original video and the delayed video, to generate subtitle data corresponding to speech or content of the original video, and to generate subtitle display timing information indicating a display timing of the subtitle data relative to the delayed video; and

a distribution server coupled to the communication network and configured to receive the delayed video from the delay unit and the subtitle data and the subtitle display timing information from the subtitler terminal, and to transmit, through the communication network to a viewer terminal, the delayed video together with the subtitle data and the subtitle display timing information,

wherein the viewer terminal is configured to display the delayed video and to display the subtitle data in synchronization with the delayed video based on the subtitle display timing information.

1. A method comprising:

receiving, by one or more processors, an original video stream;

generating, by the one or more processors, a delayed video stream corresponding to the original video stream and delayed by a delay interval;

transmitting, by the one or more processors, the original video stream to a subtitling system;

receiving, by the one or more processors from the subtitling system, subtitle data associated with the original video stream and delay information corresponding to generation of the subtitle data;

determining, by the one or more processors, presentation timing for the subtitle data based at least in part on the delay interval and the delay information; and

transmitting, by the one or more processors, the delayed video stream and the subtitle data to one or more viewer devices, wherein the subtitle data is configured to be presented with the delayed video stream according to the determined presentation timing.

1. A method for providing a video to a viewer terminal, the method being performed by a video providing apparatus comprising a communication unit and a controller, the method comprising:

receiving, by the communication unit, a request for video content from the viewer terminal;

generating, by the controller, a delayed video signal corresponding to the video content, the delayed video signal being delayed by a predetermined delay time relative to an original video signal;

receiving, by the communication unit, a subtitle signal from a subtitler terminal, the subtitle signal including subtitle data generated based on the original video signal;

determining, by the controller, display timing of the subtitle data based on the predetermined delay time of the delayed video signal;

synchronizing, by the controller, the subtitle signal with the delayed video signal according to the determined display timing; and

transmitting, by the communication unit, the delayed video signal and the synchronized subtitle signal to the viewer terminal such that the viewer terminal displays subtitles corresponding to the subtitle data in synchronization with display of the delayed video signal.

1. A computer-implemented method for live broadcast subtitling, comprising:

receiving, by one or more computing devices, a live audiovisual broadcast feed comprising video content and associated audio content;

providing the audio content, or data derived from the audio content, to a subtitling system configured to generate subtitle text corresponding to speech in the audio content;

generating, by the subtitling system, one or more subtitle items, each subtitle item including subtitle text and timing information associated with a corresponding portion of the live audiovisual broadcast feed;

buffering, by the one or more computing devices, the video content of the live audiovisual broadcast feed for a delay interval selected to accommodate at least a processing latency of the subtitling system;

delaying delivery of the video content to a viewer device by the delay interval to produce a delayed video feed;

synchronizing the one or more subtitle items with the delayed video feed based at least in part on the timing information; and

transmitting, to the viewer device, the delayed video feed and the synchronized one or more subtitle items such that the subtitle text is displayed at the viewer device substantially concurrently with the corresponding portion of the delayed video feed.
